00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:03,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:04,046 --> 00:00:07,992
Miyata, when was the last time
you wore a kimono?

2
00:00:07,992 --> 00:00:11,645
Hmm, I don't really remember.

3
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:14,701
There aren't many chances to wear one.

4
00:00:14,701 --> 00:00:19,089
You're at an age
where you should own at least one kimono.

5
00:00:19,089 --> 00:00:20,375
Yeah, yeah.

6
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:25,417
Is this for a specific occasion?

7
00:00:25,417 --> 00:00:26,902
A dinner with a friend.

8
00:00:27,629 --> 00:00:31,448
In that case, for this season,
I'd recommend a kinagashi.

9
00:00:32,697 --> 00:00:34,294
Kinagashi?

10
00:00:34,294 --> 00:00:36,858
Shall I bring one in your size?

11
00:00:36,858 --> 00:00:39,653
I don't need one. Just for him.

12
00:00:39,653 --> 00:00:40,732
Understood.

13
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:48,699
I've never had traditional Japanese clothing
as a dress code before.

14
00:00:48,699 --> 00:00:50,762
Kyosuke really has elevated tastes, huh?

15
00:00:52,055 --> 00:00:54,095
That doesn't seem like him, though.

16
00:00:55,429 --> 00:00:56,429
You think?

17
00:00:57,182 --> 00:01:02,592
I mean, he usually
only talks about wine, cheese,

18
00:01:02,592 --> 00:01:07,067
and French food
with impossibly complicated names.

19
00:01:07,878 --> 00:01:08,878
That's true.

20
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:12,435
Sorry to keep you waiting.

21
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:18,300
This fabric is made from a Shantung weave
with a distinctive luster,

22
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:22,418
and the elegant fresh green color
should feel refreshing even in summer.

23
00:01:22,418 --> 00:01:23,418
Okay.

24
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:28,863
Isn't it a bit flashy?

25
00:01:31,495 --> 00:01:33,227
You won't know untill you try it on.

26
00:01:35,216 --> 00:01:37,085
We'll try it on, please.

27
00:01:37,085 --> 00:01:38,515
Certainly.

28
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:39,858
This way, please.

29
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,458
Um...

30
00:02:14,363 --> 00:02:15,363
How does it look?

31
00:02:18,824 --> 00:02:20,133
Just as I thought.

32
00:02:21,148 --> 00:02:22,809
Traditional clothing suits you.

33
00:02:25,968 --> 00:02:28,607
It's actually more comfortable
than I expected.

34
00:02:31,606 --> 00:02:33,713
It looks wonderful on you.

35
00:02:33,713 --> 00:02:35,862
I'll bring another obi as well.

36
00:02:35,862 --> 00:02:37,224
Thank you.

37
00:02:39,449 --> 00:02:42,955
All thanks to Kyosuke's whim, I guess.

38
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:51,839
It looks beautiful.

39
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:01,890
Thanks.

40
00:03:52,498 --> 00:03:53,887
I like this vibe.

41
00:03:53,887 --> 00:03:54,887
Yeah.

42
00:03:55,983 --> 00:03:57,570
Great for a temple visit.

43
00:04:01,136 --> 00:04:02,978
The weather is really nice too.

44
00:04:02,978 --> 00:04:05,388
Yeah. The breeze feels great.

45
00:04:05,388 --> 00:04:06,646
Feels great.

46
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:09,917
Should we take a look?

47
00:04:11,378 --> 00:04:17,549
Hmm, maybe I'll buy some
as side dishes for dinner.

48
00:04:19,121 --> 00:04:23,114
Everything looks so good.
Let's get all of them.

49
00:04:23,114 --> 00:04:24,283
That's too much.

50
00:04:27,483 --> 00:04:29,853
Excuse me, can I have one of these?

51
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,125
- Of course.
- Thank you.

52
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:32,648
Thanks.

53
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:34,200
I'll try the black soybeans too.

54
00:04:41,187 --> 00:04:43,325
Mmm! Delicious.

55
00:04:50,977 --> 00:04:53,984
Wow, the sound is nice too.

56
00:04:53,984 --> 00:04:55,086
It really is.

57
00:05:32,456 --> 00:05:34,908
But man, it's so hot!

58
00:05:34,908 --> 00:05:36,412
How about a folding fan?

59
00:05:36,412 --> 00:05:38,882
Good idea. Very elegant.

60
00:05:38,882 --> 00:05:40,757
There's a shop with them up ahead.

61
00:05:42,571 --> 00:05:45,053
Takashi!

62
00:05:49,821 --> 00:05:50,821
Rui?

63
00:05:51,824 --> 00:05:53,104
<i>But that's his first name.</i>

64
00:05:53,104 --> 00:05:55,439
I'm so surprised!

65
00:05:55,439 --> 00:05:57,941
- What a coincidence.
- What are you doing here?

66
00:05:58,692 --> 00:05:59,902
I was out shopping.

67
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:05,413
Man, I'm so glad I came to Jindaiji today!

68
00:06:07,798 --> 00:06:10,542
And who's this?

69
00:06:14,402 --> 00:06:15,583
My boyfriend.

70
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:18,893
<i>He's never introduced me like that before.</i>

71
00:06:18,893 --> 00:06:21,631
Wow, you two look great together!

72
00:06:22,445 --> 00:06:24,718
Nice to meet you. I'm Miyata.

73
00:06:25,842 --> 00:06:27,179
So, what about you, Rui?

74
00:06:28,539 --> 00:06:31,433
We're on a date too.

75
00:06:32,965 --> 00:06:34,721
Hi, I'm Sho.

76
00:06:34,721 --> 00:06:35,968
Nice to meet you.

77
00:06:36,901 --> 00:06:39,608
Is this the guy you mentioned before?

78
00:06:40,537 --> 00:06:41,985
Yeah, my ex.

79
00:06:43,076 --> 00:06:44,095
<i>Another one?</i>

80
00:06:46,075 --> 00:06:50,406
He said you were a hot older guy,
and he was right.

81
00:06:50,406 --> 00:06:51,406
Thanks.

82
00:06:53,110 --> 00:06:56,270
Oh! Hey, want to do a double date?

83
00:06:57,548 --> 00:06:58,659
Huh?

84
00:06:58,659 --> 00:07:01,451
I mean, isn't it more fun with more people?

85
00:07:02,425 --> 00:07:04,382
And I haven't seen Takashi in a while.

86
00:07:08,293 --> 00:07:10,353
I don't know...

87
00:07:12,808 --> 00:07:14,615
- Rui.
- Hm?

88
00:07:14,615 --> 00:07:16,270
Let's just do the two of us today.

89
00:07:17,586 --> 00:07:19,397
Aw...

90
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,149
I want to be alone with you.

91
00:07:23,014 --> 00:07:25,612
Fine, I get it.

92
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:29,042
Well, see you around, Takashi!

93
00:07:29,042 --> 00:07:31,393
- Okay.
- You too, Miyata.

94
00:07:48,612 --> 00:07:51,659
Is this another ex-boyfriend?

95
00:07:52,732 --> 00:07:54,140
So many coincidences.

96
00:07:56,064 --> 00:07:58,425
Senpai, how many lovers have you had?

97
00:08:01,863 --> 00:08:03,150
That's a secret.

98
00:08:07,828 --> 00:08:11,324
Don't they say that not knowing
makes the relationship last longer?

99
00:08:13,266 --> 00:08:16,025
<i>Am I being too nosy?</i>

100
00:08:17,508 --> 00:08:21,589
<i>The time we spent apart
is weighing more on me now.</i>

101
00:08:23,985 --> 00:08:26,113
<i>Maybe I'm more narrow-minded
than I thought.</i>

102
00:08:28,124 --> 00:08:30,719
You went quiet, Miyata.

103
00:08:33,003 --> 00:08:35,974
Maybe the heat is melting my brain.

104
00:08:38,266 --> 00:08:41,407
The shop is just ahead. Hang in there.

105
00:08:50,197 --> 00:08:51,319
Oh!

106
00:08:52,178 --> 00:08:53,580
Found it.

107
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:57,984
Hmm.

108
00:08:58,976 --> 00:09:02,667
This would match your kimono nicely.

109
00:09:03,472 --> 00:09:05,003
Oh?

110
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:08,095
Yeah, the colors and material. See?

111
00:09:10,225 --> 00:09:15,129
I don't really get it,
but at least it's refreshing.

112
00:09:22,281 --> 00:09:24,309
Another treasure.

113
00:09:24,309 --> 00:09:26,091
- They're adding up.
- Thanks.

114
00:09:26,091 --> 00:09:27,646
I'm happy.

115
00:09:27,646 --> 00:09:29,185
I like our matching fans.

116
00:09:29,185 --> 00:09:30,610
Yeah, me too.

117
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,580
- Let's add more.
- Yeah.

118
00:09:37,484 --> 00:09:40,830
They seem close.

119
00:09:43,071 --> 00:09:44,125
Does it bother you?

120
00:09:45,092 --> 00:09:46,092
No.

121
00:09:46,998 --> 00:09:50,930
If Rui is happy, I'm happy for him.

122
00:09:52,805 --> 00:09:55,678
<i>At least he doesn't seem
to have any lingering feelings.</i>

123
00:10:04,350 --> 00:10:07,403
<i>He must've done that with Senpai too.</i>

124
00:10:11,662 --> 00:10:13,446
Senpai, let's go this way!

125
00:10:14,272 --> 00:10:16,074
There's a place I've been wanting to try.

126
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:18,685
That's rare. You never say things like that.

127
00:10:18,685 --> 00:10:20,590
- Really?
- Yeah.

128
00:10:20,590 --> 00:10:24,832
You always just say "Anywhere is fine."

129
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,821
Even I have my moments.

130
00:10:26,821 --> 00:10:28,610
Just follow me.

131
00:10:28,610 --> 00:10:29,610
Okay.

132
00:10:31,871 --> 00:10:33,556
So many options.

133
00:10:33,556 --> 00:10:35,956
- Can't decide.
- Yeah.

134
00:10:35,956 --> 00:10:39,610
The anmitsu looks good,
or maybe the shiratama...

135
00:10:40,569 --> 00:10:44,659
There's zenzai too.
Should we get everything?

136
00:10:44,659 --> 00:10:46,319
Wait...

137
00:10:46,319 --> 00:10:48,016
Either shaved ice...

138
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,692
or anmitsu.

139
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:53,945
I don't know what to choose.

140
00:10:57,053 --> 00:11:00,159
Huh? Takashi?

141
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:02,746
Oh, Rui. We meet again.

142
00:11:02,746 --> 00:11:09,091
When we walked by the shop,
I had a strong feeling that you were here.

143
00:11:09,091 --> 00:11:10,276
And here you are!

144
00:11:11,682 --> 00:11:12,977
<i>A psychic?</i>

145
00:11:16,430 --> 00:11:17,760
<i>Or is it magic?</i>

146
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,972
- Those seats are open.
- Okay.

147
00:11:21,793 --> 00:11:22,982
Are you ready to order?

148
00:11:24,032 --> 00:11:25,560
One mitsumame, please.

149
00:11:27,397 --> 00:11:31,397
One kiwi shiratama anmitsu, please.

150
00:11:31,397 --> 00:11:33,860
Oh! I'll have the same.

151
00:11:34,609 --> 00:11:36,101
You don't need the menu?

152
00:11:36,101 --> 00:11:37,941
I mean, it looks good.

153
00:11:39,327 --> 00:11:43,763
Miyata ordered it,
so it's bound to be good, right?

154
00:11:43,763 --> 00:11:45,598
Uh... yeah...

155
00:11:49,532 --> 00:11:52,002
Thank you for waiting.

156
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,360
Thank you.

157
00:11:54,718 --> 00:11:55,636
Thank you.

158
00:11:55,636 --> 00:11:58,165
You're welcome. Enjoy.

159
00:11:59,024 --> 00:12:00,560
Thanks for the food.

160
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,772
- It's an elegant sweetness.
- Yeah.

161
00:12:19,993 --> 00:12:21,157
The kiwi is good.

162
00:12:22,888 --> 00:12:24,410
Yours looks luxurious.

163
00:12:25,241 --> 00:12:27,078
It does.

164
00:12:27,078 --> 00:12:29,415
- Can I have a shiratama?
- Sure.

165
00:12:30,186 --> 00:12:31,367
Thanks.

166
00:12:32,801 --> 00:12:34,328
Mmm, that's good.

167
00:12:35,862 --> 00:12:36,862
Hey.

168
00:12:38,175 --> 00:12:39,342
Can I have a bite?

169
00:12:41,052 --> 00:12:42,871
Say "ahh."

170
00:12:44,344 --> 00:12:45,681
Mmm, that's good!

171
00:12:46,468 --> 00:12:47,588
So cute.

172
00:12:48,343 --> 00:12:50,364
What do you want?

173
00:12:50,364 --> 00:12:51,364
A mandarin orange.

174
00:12:55,416 --> 00:12:58,035
- Senpai.
- Hm?

175
00:13:00,837 --> 00:13:02,282
Say "ahh."

176
00:13:03,234 --> 00:13:04,234
Ah?

177
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:12,785
Ah... A... Always good desserts here, huh?

178
00:13:12,785 --> 00:13:16,195
Wait, isn't this your first time here?

179
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:21,331
No, I mean, the reviews
say this place is always good.

180
00:13:21,331 --> 00:13:23,859
Oh, I see.

181
00:13:24,869 --> 00:13:26,678
- There's only one though...
- What?

182
00:13:26,678 --> 00:13:28,087
Okay, fine.

183
00:13:28,087 --> 00:13:30,753
Say "ahh."

184
00:13:31,674 --> 00:13:34,146
Ugh! So stingy!

185
00:13:35,091 --> 00:13:38,097
<i>You can't do that
in front of people normally.</i>

186
00:13:39,004 --> 00:13:40,778
<i>He's way too good at being spoiled.</i>

187
00:13:46,356 --> 00:13:47,672
Thanks for the meal.

188
00:13:47,672 --> 00:13:49,743
- Thanks for the meal.
- Thank you.

189
00:13:51,108 --> 00:13:53,599
Rui, see you around.

190
00:13:53,599 --> 00:13:55,626
Aw, you're leaving already?

191
00:13:56,376 --> 00:13:58,223
Glad you're doing well.

192
00:13:58,223 --> 00:13:59,829
You too.

193
00:13:59,829 --> 00:14:02,241
Oh, I'll DM you later!

194
00:14:02,241 --> 00:14:03,241
Okay.

195
00:14:18,609 --> 00:14:20,818
Maybe we bought too many sweets.

196
00:14:30,462 --> 00:14:32,580
Mmm, that's good.

197
00:14:35,751 --> 00:14:38,076
- Senpai.
- Hm?

198
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:44,069
Let me have that.

199
00:14:44,069 --> 00:14:45,069
Okay.

200
00:14:47,468 --> 00:14:48,468
No, not that.

201
00:14:55,864 --> 00:14:56,864
Ahh.

202
00:15:10,065 --> 00:15:11,494
Don't laugh.

203
00:15:23,891 --> 00:15:24,891
What's wrong?

204
00:15:28,653 --> 00:15:32,098
I'm feeling a little insecure.

205
00:15:39,727 --> 00:15:41,810
Because of someone that young...

206
00:15:46,093 --> 00:15:48,325
Something's wrong with me.

207
00:15:50,164 --> 00:15:52,249
By young, do you mean Rui?

208
00:15:55,414 --> 00:15:57,081
Are you jealous again?

209
00:15:58,292 --> 00:16:00,237
Yes, I'm jealous!

210
00:16:00,237 --> 00:16:02,109
You really are something else.

211
00:16:02,109 --> 00:16:03,770
Tell me.

212
00:16:03,770 --> 00:16:04,743
Huh?

213
00:16:04,743 --> 00:16:06,424
About Rui.

214
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:07,894
That's in the past.

215
00:16:07,894 --> 00:16:09,227
Don't dodge the question.

216
00:16:10,757 --> 00:16:14,724
Think about how I feel,
running into one ex after another.

217
00:16:22,341 --> 00:16:23,387
You're right.

218
00:16:25,519 --> 00:16:26,519
Okay.

219
00:16:30,034 --> 00:16:32,062
I met Rui four years ago.

220
00:16:38,737 --> 00:16:40,541
I was out on a run.

221
00:16:57,781 --> 00:16:58,781
Hello.

222
00:17:00,776 --> 00:17:02,271
Hello.

223
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:05,077
Do you run around here often?

224
00:17:05,077 --> 00:17:07,736
No, this is my first time.

225
00:17:07,736 --> 00:17:10,364
I thought so. I haven't seen you around.

226
00:17:11,626 --> 00:17:14,326
This route is nice. Easy to run.

227
00:17:15,546 --> 00:17:18,787
I'm Rui. What's your name?

228
00:17:19,792 --> 00:17:23,000
Takashi Iwanaga. Nice to meet you.

229
00:17:24,632 --> 00:17:25,632
Takashi.

230
00:17:29,264 --> 00:17:30,964
Can I have some of that?

231
00:17:30,964 --> 00:17:33,177
I already drank from it.

232
00:17:34,054 --> 00:17:36,998
That makes it even better.

233
00:17:47,423 --> 00:17:49,521
<i>Rui was a very charming person.</i>

234
00:17:50,816 --> 00:17:55,304
<i>He never held back his affection for me.</i>

235
00:17:55,304 --> 00:17:57,034
<i>He expressed it fully.</i>

236
00:17:59,716 --> 00:18:01,557
So even when we broke up,

237
00:18:02,646 --> 00:18:04,822
we didn't hide anything from each other.

238
00:18:08,252 --> 00:18:10,131
We were able to part amicably.

239
00:18:15,251 --> 00:18:22,101
I'm no good at being spoiled
or expressing my feelings anyway.

240
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,176
But you know...

241
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:30,681
I love that about you, Miyata.

242
00:18:32,091 --> 00:18:33,596
You don't need to change.

243
00:18:39,174 --> 00:18:40,578
Senpai.

244
00:18:45,987 --> 00:18:47,072
Let's try again.

245
00:18:50,239 --> 00:18:51,239
Wanna say "ahh"?

246
00:18:53,845 --> 00:18:55,676
No, thanks.

247
00:19:00,123 --> 00:19:02,741
[Book Designer Selection Workflow]

248
00:19:02,741 --> 00:19:06,554
[Documents for Book Design Planning]

249
00:19:07,439 --> 00:19:09,382
- Good work today.
- Good work.

250
00:19:10,307 --> 00:19:15,044
Miyata, how's the project
with Mr. Iwanaga going?

251
00:19:15,044 --> 00:19:16,629
It's going well.

252
00:19:16,629 --> 00:19:20,225
I'm reaching out to a few designers
for the cover.

253
00:19:21,149 --> 00:19:22,149
I see.

254
00:19:24,164 --> 00:19:25,316
Is something wrong?

255
00:19:27,445 --> 00:19:28,445
Well,

256
00:19:29,591 --> 00:19:33,541
I heard that upper management
is serious about restructuring.

257
00:19:34,455 --> 00:19:37,093
Consultants might come to our department too.

258
00:19:38,538 --> 00:19:39,887
Consultants?

259
00:19:42,099 --> 00:19:46,599
They're going to cut unprofitable projects
and staff without mercy.

260
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:53,574
We need to stay sharp.

261
00:19:56,183 --> 00:19:59,574
How about we grab a drink and vent tonight?

262
00:20:00,893 --> 00:20:03,786
Sorry, I already have plans.

263
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:05,079
A date?

264
00:20:06,116 --> 00:20:07,116
Yes.

265
00:20:08,542 --> 00:20:12,032
My apologies then. Another time.

266
00:20:12,032 --> 00:20:14,017
- Thank you.
- Bye then.

267
00:20:28,934 --> 00:20:30,466
Turn around.

268
00:20:30,466 --> 00:20:32,773
Right side first, then left.

269
00:20:56,014 --> 00:20:58,179
- Can you hold that?
- Yes.

270
00:21:30,253 --> 00:21:31,705
I'm tying it.

271
00:21:31,705 --> 00:21:32,705
Okay.

272
00:22:25,525 --> 00:22:27,767
It should be around here.

273
00:22:29,379 --> 00:22:31,893
It'd be easier
if he just shared his location.

274
00:22:33,946 --> 00:22:35,438
Oh, Kyosuke!

275
00:22:38,871 --> 00:22:39,911
Salut!

276
00:22:43,034 --> 00:22:45,774
Thank you so much for the invitation.

277
00:22:45,774 --> 00:22:47,292
It's been a while.

278
00:22:47,292 --> 00:22:49,731
Thank you for coming.

279
00:22:49,731 --> 00:22:51,495
For indulging my whims.

280
00:22:54,774 --> 00:22:57,914
Not "Yakatabune." "Yakata-bune."

281
00:22:57,914 --> 00:22:59,245
Yakatabune?

282
00:22:59,245 --> 00:23:00,421
Yakata-bune.

283
00:23:00,421 --> 00:23:02,246
- Yakata-bune.
- Yakata-bune.

284
00:23:02,246 --> 00:23:03,496
You're so strict.

285
00:23:09,812 --> 00:23:11,337
Are we the only ones on the boat?

286
00:23:11,337 --> 00:23:13,542
No, there's one more person.

287
00:23:14,651 --> 00:23:15,651
Here.

288
00:23:16,795 --> 00:23:21,358
Hello, Takashi, Miyata.

289
00:23:30,790 --> 00:23:33,996
<i>I'm the most important person to you, right?</i>

290
00:23:33,996 --> 00:23:39,201
<i>Don't you know how crazy I am about you?</i>

291
00:23:39,201 --> 00:23:42,203
I honestly can't imagine it.

292
00:23:42,203 --> 00:23:44,620
- You really are pure.
- Are you teasing me?

293
00:23:44,620 --> 00:23:46,841
<i>Aren't those two way too close?</i>

294
00:23:46,841 --> 00:23:48,939
<i>I don't really care.</i>

295
00:23:48,939 --> 00:23:51,280
I hear he's the only guy
who ever dumped Takashi.

296
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:52,936
No matter what.

297
00:23:52,936 --> 00:23:54,331
Why would you do that?

298
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:59,438
<i>That's what they call retroactive jealousy.</i>

